# Oracle probe (L11.9, ADR 0186) — containers nest. A list whose element is a list is now
# built, printed, compared and grown (roadmap L11.1 step 2, ADR 0238): the slot holds the inner
# object's handle and its tag routes the printer and rt_container_eq. What the compiled leg still
# cannot do is read a nested element back as a *value* — m[0][1] and d["a"][1] index a container
# that lives in a slot, which is the tagged element read L11.1 still owes (its last clause).
m = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
print(m[0][1])
d = {"a": [1, 2]}
print(d["a"][1])
xs = []
xs.append([7, 8])
print(len(xs))
print(xs[0][0])
